Package: loesslin
Type: Package
Title: Memory-Efficient Standard Errors for Loess Predictions
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Don", "Yin", email = "Don_Yin@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("R Core Team", role = c("ctb", "cph")),
    person(family = "Cleveland", role = "ctb"),
    person(family = "Grosse", role = "ctb"),
    person(family = "Shyu", role = "ctb"),
    person("AT&T", role = "cph"))
Description: Computes predictions and pointwise standard errors from a fit
    produced by stats::loess(), preserving the results of predict() with
    se = TRUE. For the interpolation surface, compact local fit records
    and ordered recomputation replace the quadratic native workspace.
    The direct surface retains R's standard calculation. Derived from
    the loess implementation distributed with R.
